# INERT803 snapshot entry scaffold

Based on independently source-reviewed but UNACCEPTED StageA2b0075c, from accepted802main8aaaecc. Existing803 prototype605b451 and805a1c747b branches preserved. No URL, agent tool, adapter, registry, migration or existing flow calls this module.

Internal _run_authenticated receives a server-authenticated User object, never a request-selectable actor PK, then reloads that principal inside an outer durable REPEATABLE READ transaction after first-command SET. An active context marker indicates boundary only, not authorization; callbacks must retain all native permissions. Ambient atomic/nonautocommit fails closed. Only closed803 domain sets allowed; future generic guard rejects unentered/mixed sets. Output accepts only materialized finite JSON shape. Context resets on success/failure; database conflict classification occurs outside atomic for explicit40001/40P01 only; no automatic retry, including unknown commit/connection failure. Existing lock helper is not called or modified.

Snapshot-time semantics remain an UNACCEPTED activation gate, not equivalent to through-commit revocation exclusion. No production operation callback is installed. This scaffold does NOT solve bounded private closure, nested payload admission, native permission composition, source owner-currentness, or concurrency yet. Snapshot coherence is not permission. Private JSON output budgets belong to the later admitted domain layer; materialize is not a size limiter.

Four pure tests pass normal/-O: key closure, materialization rejection, exact SQLSTATE classifier and structural boundary/reset/no-activation. Five finite native definitions discovered under ensure_connection forbidden: actual SQL ordering/fresh user, nested rejection, cached-active revocation, rollback/context reset and client-identity/mixed-domain rejection. All native definitions UNRUN. Still required before activation: real two-connection closure/policy/grant contrasts, actual confirmed serialization/deadlock rollback, unknown-commit no-retry integration, nonautocommit entry contrast, complete five operation routes and native idempotence tests. No DB execution or isolation change performed during development.

Independent-review hardening: nondefault aliases reject before any connection lookup, because existing native callback queries use default. Principal deletion between initial server authentication and snapshot reload maps to fixed PermissionDenied, no DoesNotExist leakage. Trusted internal callbacks explicitly forbid lazy returns/on_commit hooks/provider/external effects; this is not a sandbox for arbitrary callbacks. Five pure tests normal/-O and DB-forbidden static/exact-seven discovery pass. Seven native definitions remain UNRUN; no production activation. Prior3ef88b preserved in history.
